# ScholarPath – Architecture Plan v3


## 1. System Vision

ScholarPath is a **decision + execution intelligence platform for students**.

The system evolves through three tightly coupled layers:

* Phase 7 → Recommendation Engine (Intelligence)
* Phase 8 → Action Engine (Decision Layer)
* Phase 9 → Integration Layer (External Data Ingestion)

---

## 2. Core Architectural Principle

> The Action Engine is the single source of truth for user prioritization.

No other system may define “what the user should do next”.

---

## 3. High-Level System Architecture

```text id="arch1"
[ Next.js Frontend ]
        ↓
[ Action Engine (Phase 8) ]   ← PRIMARY DECISION LAYER
        ↓
[ Recommendation Engine (Phase 7) ]
        ↓
[ Matching Engine ]
        ↓
[ PostgreSQL Database ]
        ↓
[ AI Layer (Claude API) ]
        ↓
[ External Integration Layer (Phase 9) ]
```

---

## 4. Phase Boundaries

### Phase 7 – Recommendation Engine (Intelligence Layer)

Responsibilities:

* Generate scholarship recommendations
* Compute relevance scoring
* Rank opportunities
* Emit recommendation events

Constraints:

* No user prioritization
* No action creation
* No UI decisions

Output:

* Ranked recommendation set

---

### Phase 8 – Action Engine (Decision Layer)

Responsibilities:

* Convert system signals into Actions
* Prioritize user actions deterministically
* Maintain Action lifecycle
* Enforce deduplication rules
* Serve dashboard feed

Constraints:

* No AI-based decision making
* No external system calls
* No direct business logic outside priority rules

Output:

* UserAction list (source of truth for UI)

---

### Phase 9 – External Integration Layer (Data Layer)

Responsibilities:

* Fetch external data sources:

  * Scholarships
  * Jobs
  * Universities
* Normalize external data into internal schema
* Emit structured events into system

Constraints:

* Read-only from external systems
* User-assisted flow only
* No submission to external systems

Output:

* ExternalDataEvents → internal event stream

---

