## 6. Data Ownership Model

| Domain               | Owner        |
| -------------------- | ------------ |
| User Profile         | Core System  |
| Applications         | Core System  |
| Recommendations      | Phase 7      |
| Actions              | Phase 8      |
| External Data        | Phase 9      |
| Prioritization Logic | Phase 8 ONLY |

---

## 7. System Invariants (Hard Rules)

* There is only ONE source of truth for prioritization (Action Engine)
* No duplicate OPEN Actions per user/entity/type
* External systems cannot mutate internal state directly
* AI cannot influence priority logic
* UI is a consumer only, never a decision maker

---

## 8. Action Engine Contract (Phase 8 Core)

### Action Lifecycle

```text id="life1"
OPEN → DONE
OPEN → DISMISSED
OPEN → EXPIRED
```

---

### Deduplication Rule

```text id="dedup1"
(user_id + action_type + related_entity_id) = UNIQUE OPEN ACTION
```

---

### Expiration Rules

* DEADLINE_ACTION → expires after deadline
* COMPLETION_ACTION → closes when completed
* OPPORTUNITY_ACTION → expires after 30 days
* ENGAGEMENT_ACTION → expires after 14 days
* OPTIMIZATION_ACTION → expires after 30 days or resolution

---

### Priority Principle

Priority is computed based on:

* urgency
* impact
* completion_gap
* engagement

With business-level overrides (not hardcoded constants).

---

## 9. Recalculation Strategy

Action Engine recalculates on:

* Profile updates
* Application updates
* Recommendation generation
* Nightly reconciliation job

Guarantee:

> System reflects meaningful changes in near real-time while maintaining stability.

---

## 10. Consistency Model

### Phase 7 (Recommendations)

* Eventual consistency acceptable

### Phase 8 (Actions)

* Strong consistency per user

### Phase 9 (External Data)

* Eventual consistency only

---

## 11. Failure Model

* Phase 7 failure → fallback to cached recommendations
* Phase 8 failure → freeze action updates, serve last known state
* Phase 9 failure → system operates on internal data only

---

## 12. API Surface (Core)

### Actions API

```text id="api1"
GET /actions
```

Supports:

* filtering (type, status)
* sorting (priority_score, deadline)
* pagination

Constraint:

> API never computes priority — only serves Action Engine output.

---

## 13. UI Data Model

Dashboard is driven by:

1. Action Center (Primary)
2. Recommendations (Secondary)
3. Deadlines & Risks (Supporting)

Max visible Actions:

* 5 items

---

## 14. System Invariants Enforcement

These rules are non-negotiable:

* No duplicate OPEN actions
* No external write-back to internal DB
* No AI-based ranking override
* No bypassing Action Engine
* No UI-based prioritization logic

---

## 15. Versioning Strategy

* Phase logic is versioned
* Scoring model is configurable (not hardcoded)
* Backward compatibility required for:

  * Actions
  * Events
  * External data schemas

---

## 16. Non-Functional Requirements

* ≤ 500 users (MVP stage)
* API latency < 2.5s
* AI async tolerance ≤ 20s
* System must function without AI dependency
* Deterministic outputs required across runs

---

## 17. Future Evolution

### Phase 10+ Vision

* Predictive Action Engine (pre-event actions)
* ML-based priority tuning
* Cross-platform integrations
* Adaptive personalization of scoring model

---

## 18. Final Architectural Statement

> ScholarPath is not a recommendation system.
> It is a deterministic decision system that converts external signals into prioritized user actions.
